# SaaS Starter Kit — agent rules

Next.js 16 + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind 3 + Auth.js v5 + Prisma + Postgres. Billing via Polar or Stripe. See `AGENTS.md` for the full tour.

## Commands (all must pass before a commit)

- `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`
- `npm run dev` — local server on http://localhost:3000

## Layout

- Pages: `src/app/` (`/`, `/pricing`, `/docs`, `/blog`, `/changelog`, `/auth/*`, `/dashboard/*`)
- Auth: `src/auth.ts`, `src/proxy.ts` (Next.js 16 — not `middleware.ts`)
- Billing: `src/lib/polar.ts`, `src/lib/stripe.ts`, `src/app/api/checkout/`, `src/app/api/webhooks/`
- Email: `src/lib/email.ts` (Resend)
- Blog: `src/lib/blog.ts`, `src/content/blog/*.mdx`
- Database: `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts`

## Hard rules

- `DATABASE_URL` must be the Supabase **session pooler (port 5432)** — never the transaction pooler (6543). The transaction pooler hangs `prisma db push` and breaks Prisma at runtime (42P05).
- Session cookie: over HTTPS Auth.js sets `__Secure-authjs.session-token`; tell `getToken()` the name or login loops forever.
- Login/signup pages are `force-dynamic` — never statically prerender them.
- No demo login, no invented testimonials, counts, or revenue. Empty states say so honestly.
- No secrets in code or git — env vars only.
- Reuse `src/components/ui.tsx` (Button, Card, Badge, SectionHeading) — no one-off primitives.
